// Typecheck project for the serverless API.
//
// ## Why this file exists
//
// Until it was added, NOTHING type-checked the production API. The root
// `tsconfig.json` has `"files": []` and references only `tsconfig.app.json`
// (`include: ["src"]`), `tsconfig.node.json` (`include: ["vite.config.ts"]`)
// and the two workspace packages, and CI ran exactly the first two
// (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`). An `api/tsconfig.json` existed but was
// referenced by nothing and run by nothing; it has been deleted in favour of
// this file so there is one config for this tree, sitting next to the two
// configs CI already knows how to run.
//
// The cost of that gap was `server-handlers/auth/me.ts`, which called
// `createApiHandler({ routes: [...] })` when the function takes a method-keyed
// object. `routes['GET']` was `undefined`, so `GET /api/auth/me` answered 405
// to every request in production from the day it was written. It is a plain
// excess-property error — one `tsc` run away from being impossible.
//
// ## What this project covers
//
//   api/**             the catch-all dispatcher
//   lib/**             services, middleware, config, types
//   server-handlers/** all 37 production handlers
//
// `packages/backend/**` and `packages/shared/**` are pulled in transitively via
// imports (e.g. `AuthService`, `jwt`), so they are checked here too.
//
// ## Deliberately relaxed compiler options
//
// `strict` is ON. Two of its sub-flags are turned back off, and both are
// temporary — the reason each is off is a fact about the current tree, not a
// preference:
//
//   "useUnknownInCatchVariables": false
//       151 errors. Every handler and service is written `catch (error) { ...
//       error.message ... }`. Fixing it means editing ~25 files including
//       `lib/services/TagService.ts` and `server-handlers/tags/merge.ts`.
//
//   "strictNullChecks": false
//       55 errors with it on, of which 11 sit in files that cannot be touched
//       right now (`lib/services/AttachmentService.ts`,
//       `lib/services/TagService.ts` — `rowCount` is `number | null` in
//       @types/pg, and `TagEntity` omits the timestamp columns). The rest are
//       null/undefined mismatches inside service business logic
//       (`EventService` 696/713-718, `CalendarService` 427/444) that deserve
//       their own pass rather than being swept up in a config change.
//
// Everything else strict stays on, including `noImplicitAny` and
// `strictFunctionTypes` — those cost only five mechanical fixes, so leaving
// them on was cheap and makes this a materially stronger gate.
//
// To tighten later: flip `strictNullChecks` first (it is the bigger win), fix
// the ~55 sites, then `useUnknownInCatchVariables`.
//
// ## What this gate can and cannot catch
//
// It DOES reject the `me.ts` shape: excess-property checking is not a strict
// flag, so `createApiHandler({ routes: [...] })` is TS2353 even here. Its
// limit is that excess-property checking only fires on a *fresh object literal*
// at the call site — a hoisted `const cfg = { routes: [...] }` would pass,
// because `Partial<Record<HttpMethod, RouteConfig>>` has no required keys and
// `{}` is assignable to it. That is why the runtime test in
// `server-handlers/auth/__tests__/me.test.ts` exists as a second, independent
// gate. Neither replaces the other.
//
// Tests are excluded, matching `tsconfig.app.json`.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "NodeNext",
    "moduleResolution": "NodeNext",
    "lib": ["ES2022"],

    "strict": true,
    "useUnknownInCatchVariables": false,
    "strictNullChecks": false,

    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": false,
    "noUnusedParameters": false,
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@shared/*": ["./packages/shared/src/*"],
      "@lib/*": ["./lib/*"],
      "@api/*": ["./api/*"]
    },
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["api/**/*.ts", "lib/**/*.ts", "server-handlers/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "**/*.test.ts", "**/__tests__/**"]
}
